1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,135
The cost of the renegotiated roles arrived as a letter.

2
00:00:03,135 --> 00:00:11,050
The three of them had promised to be at every Thursday meeting; by the third week, one of them was not there.

3
00:00:11,050 --> 00:00:15,300
“I cannot be in two places,” Lin said.

4
00:00:15,300 --> 00:00:17,790
“This is not a gesture.

5
00:00:17,790 --> 00:00:28,476
I am telling you what is true.” His grandmother was in hospital, and the trial of the new care plan fell in the same week.

6
00:00:28,476 --> 00:00:32,316
Maya took the minutes alone for three weeks.

7
00:00:32,316 --> 00:00:36,821
“The majority of the work is invisible,” she wrote.

8
00:00:36,821 --> 00:00:50,432
“A trustee of a small thing is a guardian of other people's time.” She was sure of one point only: a promise that depends on one person is not a promise, it is a hope.

9
00:00:50,432 --> 00:00:56,227
Her will was stronger than his schedule, and both of them knew it.

10
00:00:56,227 --> 00:01:05,627
A man from the mill, an old friend of his grandfather, came to the house on the eve of the funeral and spoke about trust.

11
00:01:05,627 --> 00:01:09,742
“Your grandfather was a radical,” he said.

12
00:01:09,742 --> 00:01:22,673
“He burned the lease in the yard, and three families kept their homes because of it.” It was a model of a certain kind of courage, and it was also a warning.

13
00:01:22,673 --> 00:01:27,788
At the grave, an uncle and two aunts stood with the children.

14
00:01:27,788 --> 00:01:40,119
“Yes,” his auntie said, “he was a proper witness to a bad century.” A violent storm came up, and the Medicare papers in his bag got wet.

15
00:01:40,119 --> 00:01:45,529
“You cannot substitute a plan for a person,” his mother said.

16
00:01:45,529 --> 00:01:51,854
“That is the profound part, and it is the part nobody writes down.”

17
00:01:51,854 --> 00:02:01,419
He went back to the dormitory and wrote himself a note: do not lose the thread, and do not bribe yourself with busyness.

18
00:02:01,419 --> 00:02:09,199
A desperate week is not a failure; it is a critical week, and judgment is easy from the outside.

19
00:02:09,199 --> 00:02:16,669
His peer group — a friendly cyclist and a young woman from the third floor — offered to guard the Thursday slot.

20
00:02:16,669 --> 00:02:20,550
“The return will be slow,” Maya said.

21
00:02:20,550 --> 00:02:23,090
“Be sure that it happens.

22
00:02:23,090 --> 00:02:33,240
Ask yourself what you would tackle first if you had one clear shot at it.” All of those promises were still on the board when he left.

23
00:02:33,240 --> 00:02:42,601
“I hear you,” he said, “and here is what I can carry.” Him, of all people, she trusted.

24
00:02:42,601 --> 00:02:49,301
People came and went; the ones who stayed were the ones who said honestly what they could hold.

25
00:02:49,301 --> 00:02:53,041
He wanted to see whether the promise would hold.

26
00:02:53,041 --> 00:03:02,744
He watched the others go away down the corridor and understood that obedience to a timetable is not the same as loyalty.
